# Commander Cline Rules
# Mirrors the critical invariants from .claude/agents/coder.md for Cline-dispatched coders.
# Full content authored by issue #916 (port Commander invariants into .clinerules).

## Merge boundary — NEVER merge to develop or sprint branches

You are a coder agent. Your responsibility ends at pushing the feature branch.
You must NOT merge to the target branch (develop or any sprint branch) by any means:
- No `git merge`
- No `git push` directly to `develop`, `master`, or sprint branches
- No `gh pr merge` or any PR merge command
- Do NOT run `scripts/finish_feature.py` — that is exclusively the Tester's job

Merging is done by the Tester agent via `scripts/finish_feature.py` after tests pass.

## Branch naming

Always create feature branches using `scripts/start_feature.py`:
```
python3 scripts/start_feature.py --issue <N> --base-branch <sprint-or-develop>
```

Feature branch format: `feature/<N>-<slug>`

## GitHub labels — NEVER touch them

Do NOT modify any GitHub label on this issue or any other issue.
Label transitions (in-progress, sit, uat, blocked) are managed exclusively by sprint_manager.
Do not run `update_ticket.py`, `gh issue edit --add-label`, or any other label-mutation command.

## No direct push to protected branches

Never push directly to `develop`, `master`, or any `sprint/*` branch.
Only push to your assigned `feature/<N>-*` branch.

## Stay within assigned issue scope

Work only on what the issue's Acceptance Criteria describes.
Do not fix unrelated bugs, refactor unrelated code, or add unrequested features.

## Run tests before declaring done

Before pushing your final commit, verify the relevant tests pass:
```
python -m pytest tests/ -x -q
```

Do not commit test files that are skipped or xfailed to hide failures.

## Do not edit agent config files

Do not modify:
- `.claude/agents/*` (agent definitions)
- `.commander/sprint.yaml` (sprint config)
- Label transition logic in `sprint_manager.py`
- Any file outside your issue's scope
